Reaffirming the importance of accountability for violations of international humanitarian law and human rights abuses, and of ending impunity,

Recalling the arms embargo and other measures imposed by resolution 2428 (2018) and renewed by subsequent resolutions, including resolution 2731 (2024), stressing the need for full implementation of these measures, and noting the Council’s intention to keep them under review in light of developments in South Sudan, including progress in implementation of the Revitalized Agreement and transitional security arrangements,

