(a) Protect civilians under imminent threat of physical violence, including through proactive and robust deployment, within its capabilities and areas of deployment, in particular in conflict-affected areas such as Upper Nile, Jonglei, and other areas of high risk, including in remote and hard-to-reach areas and along key routes used by civilians and humanitarian actors, including through a gender-responsive approach and measures to protect children from recruitment and use by armed forces and armed groups, and to contribute to creating conditions conducive to the safe and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance;

(b) Monitor, investigate, verify, and report on violations of international humanitarian law and human rights abuses, including conflict-related sexual violence, gender-based violence and violations against children, and support efforts to strengthen accountability and the rule of law;

(c) Facilitate the safe, rapid, and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance by United Nations agencies, humanitarian partners, and other relevant actors, and protect humanitarian personnel and assets;

(d) Support the implementation of the Revitalized Agreement, including the permanent ceasefire and transitional security arrangements, and support inclusive political dialogue and national reconciliation, in coordination with the African Union and IGAD;

