(f) Support the protection of civilians and promote respect for human rights, including by engaging with the Government of South Sudan, the opposition, and armed groups;

3. Authorizes UNMISS to take all necessary measures, within its capabilities and areas of deployment, to protect civilians and to carry out its mandate, in strict compliance with the Charter of the United Nations and the Status of Forces Agreement and in full respect for the sovereignty, independence, territorial integrity and national unity of South Sudan, consistent with this mandate and, as appropriate, in coordination with the Government of South Sudan, and requests UNMISS to prioritize the protection of civilians;

4. Demands that all parties immediately cease hostilities, in particular in Nasir and Upper Nile State, withdraw forces from populated areas, exercise maximum restraint, and engage in dialogue through existing ceasefire mechanisms and political processes, and calls on all armed groups to refrain from violence and to resolve grievances peacefully;

5. Demands that all parties, including the Government of South Sudan, ensure safe, rapid, unhindered, and sustained access for UNMISS and humanitarian actors to all areas of South Sudan, including across conflict lines and across borders, including by removing arbitrary bureaucratic impediments and expediting administrative approvals, and cooperate fully with UNMISS, in accordance with the Status of Forces Agreement, including by ensuring the safety and security of its personnel and assets;

6. Condemns all attacks on civilians, humanitarian personnel, and United Nations personnel, as well as the recruitment and use of children and conflict-related sexual violence, and demands that the perpetrators of the recent clashes in Nasir and all other violations, including conflict-related sexual violence and grave violations against children, be held accountable, including through independent, impartial and credible investigations and, as appropriate, prosecution of those responsible in accordance with national law and applicable international obligations, while respecting the sovereignty and national jurisdiction of South Sudan and supporting national accountability and rule-of-law institutions, and urges the Government of South Sudan to cooperate fully with relevant regional and international accountability mechanisms, as appropriate;

7. Calls on the Government of South Sudan and the opposition to fully implement the Revitalized Agreement, including by expediting transitional security arrangements, completing the constitution-making process, creating the necessary conditions for inclusive and credible elections, and ensuring the full, equal, meaningful and safe participation of women, youth, persons with disabilities, and civil society in constitution-making, transitional arrangements, political dialogue and elections, and to ensure an enabling environment for civil society, media, and political actors, including freedom of expression and assembly, in accordance with South Sudan’s legal framework and applicable international obligations, with the support of the African Union and IGAD, as appropriate;

8. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to review the configuration and resources of UNMISS, in close consultation with troop- and police-contributing countries and the Government of South Sudan, to ensure the efficient and effective implementation of its mandate, and to provide the Council with comprehensive reports every 90 days on the implementation of the UNMISS mandate, including on the protection of civilians, humanitarian access and obstructions thereto, human rights, political developments, preparations for elections, implementation of the women, peace and security and children and armed conflict agendas, violations of the arms embargo imposed by resolution 2428 (2018) and renewed by resolution 2731 (2024), the safety and security of UNMISS personnel and measures taken to enhance the protection of peacekeepers, cooperation with the African Union and IGAD, and the situation in Upper Nile and efforts to address the recent clashes in Nasir, including conflict-related sexual violence and violations and abuses against children, as well as the regional impact, including refugee flows and cross-border security;

